failure.message:
org.junit.ComparisonFailure: expected:<[]не́кто is an indefin...> but was:<[кто — никто́. что — ничто́. The first pair concerns a person and nobody; the second concerns a thing and nothing. The indefinite options не́кто and не́что refer to an unspecified person or thing, not the corresponding nobody/nothing form. Do not treat a similar-looking prefix as proof of the same meaning.

Negative predicative constructions express the absence of a person or thing for an action. The construction selects a case form; it has no nominative form. Compare the indefinite pronoun separately. не́кого спросить — there is nobody to ask. This is absence of a person available for the infinitive action; it differs from an unspecified person and from there is nothing to ask.

]не́кто is an indefin...>

